.th SETMNT VIII 5/31/77
.sh NAME
setmnt \- establish mnttab table
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd /etc/setmnt
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Setmnt
creates the
.bd /etc/mnttab
table (see
.it mnttab\^\c
(V)), which is needed for both the
.it mount\^\c
(VIII) and
.it umount\^\c
(VIII) commands.
.it Setmnt
reads standard input,
and creates a
.it mnttab
entry for each line.
Input lines have the format:
.s3
.in +5n
filesys node
.in -5n
.s3
where
.it filesys
is the name of the file system's
.it "special file"
(e.g., ``rp??''),
and
.it node
is the root name of that file system.
Thus
.it filesys
and
.it node
become the first two strings
in the
.it mnttab\^\c
(V) entry.
.sh FILES
/etc/mnttab
.sh "SEE ALSO"
mnttab(V)
.sh "BUGS"
Evil things will happen if
.it filesys
or
.it node
are longer than 10 characters.
.s3
.it Setmnt
silently enforces an upper limit on the maximum number of
.it mnttab
entries.
